\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Using Tor
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Connecting to Tor
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
When you first launch Tor,
 you will be presented with a screen for configuring your Tor session.
 If you are not connected to the Wifi or a network,
 do that first.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Graphics
	filename images/ConnectingToTor.png
	scale 30

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In the following menu,
 select 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Connect to Tor Automatically
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

.
 You will be given the option to connect with a Tor bridge.
 Tor bridges are essentially a VPN for the first hop of the Tor circuit,
 providing a way to access the Tor network in countries that block it,
 or if you want to hide from your ISP you are using Tor.
 This may or may not be necessary given your threat model and risk tolerance.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Graphics
	filename images/ConnectToTorDefaults.png
	scale 30

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Hit 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Connect
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 and the system will begin setting up your Tor circuit.
 It may take several minutes to complete.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Graphics
	filename images/ConnectToTorInProgress.png
	scale 30

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Sites that Block Tor
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Some sites block access from the Tor network.
 One thing you can try is to use a new Tor circuit.
 Not all Tor exit nodes may be blocked by the site you are trying to visit.
 To request a new Tor circuit,
 select the options menu in the top right hand corner of the Tor browser,
 and select 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

New Tor Circuit for this Site
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Note,
 if you are trying to start a new session to preserve anonymity,
 it is safer to restart Tor completely or restart Tails.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Graphics
	filename images/NewTorCircuitCropped.png
	scale 30

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Preserving Anonymity
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Tails can't preserve your anonymity online if you supply information that identifies you.
 If you are trying to remain anonymous during your session,
 don't log into any accounts that you use on other devices.
 If you create an account inside of a Tor session,
 don't log into that account outside of Tor.
 
\end_layout

